WEBVTT

00:02:30.271 --> 00:02:34.233
And there’s the conflict zone,
with its waste of resources and goodwill.

00:02:37.612 --> 00:02:39.322
We can see these patterns at work

00:02:39.363 --> 00:02:42.283
in many of our emerging planetary crises.

00:02:42.325 --> 00:02:46.245
The transition to new energy, food
and transport systems, for instance,

00:02:46.245 --> 00:02:48.289
all demand that we meet our current needs

00:02:48.331 --> 00:02:51.584
while also adapting towards
a more sustainable future.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.296
Dilemma thinking invites us
to take situations

00:02:55.338 --> 00:02:58.007
where we're stuck between opposing values

00:02:58.049 --> 00:03:01.385
and to create a space
where both have something to contribute,